From: Teather maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] honor packet-information setting on Linux

tun2proxy 0.8.3 passes `false` for packet information from its CLI but ignores
that value on Linux and tells the tun crate to expect the four-byte PI header.
That corrupts packets when an inherited descriptor was created with IFF_NO_PI.
Honor the existing API argument as the other Unix platforms already do. Remove
this patch when an upstream release contains the equivalent fix.

--- a/src/general_api.rs
+++ b/src/general_api.rs
@@ -122,6 +122,6 @@ pub async fn general_run_async(
     #[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
     tun_config.platform_config(|cfg| {
         #[allow(deprecated)]
-        cfg.packet_information(true);
+        cfg.packet_information(_packet_information);
         cfg.ensure_root_privileges(args.setup);
     });
